      "side": 1,
      "message": "On the client side, the `HostKeyAlgorithms` field can be used to select allowable signature algorithms. There\u0027s no good option on the server side -- either we support the algorithm, or we don\u0027t. This didn\u0027t matter before because you could filter by `ssh.PublicKey.Type()` in the `PublicKeyCallback`, but now there\u0027s no way to say \"I want SHA-2 RSA pubkey signatures, but not SHA-1\". I\u0027m not sure how to expose this configuration but it\u0027s clearly desirable.",
      "revId": "529275081d22a0282b1c5ccd137ffab21180d419",
